// What the forage screen reads and notices (the old ForageFeature, ForageClueVariant, ScavengeScenarioVariant,
// WorkRunner and ForageStrategy texts and numbers). Loaded once by Content.
//
// quality: the ground's word for its density (old ForageDensity), highest first: the first whose atLeast
//   the density reaches. failures: what an empty search says, by the band the ground's word is in.
// luck: the mood line for a search's luck (one roll a search, Pools.Luck); Normal says nothing.
// hints: the sub-category word a focus shows for each resource it would look for (old GetSubCategory).
// clues: what a forager may notice before searching, drawn by weight (Clues.At). kind: Resource clues name the
//   resources they promise and multiply them by yield when the matching focus is chosen; Game clues wait for
//   small game; Negative clues cut the whole search by yield; Scavenge clues leave bone scraps (no animals) or,
//   on a roll (Work.ScavengeCarcassPct), a carcass of one of their animals that ranges near (eaten harvestedPct;
//   frozen: frozen through) when the search ends, once a draw. when: what must be true of the place,
//   the sky or the animals near for it to be drawn at all. A Resource clue's weight is scaled by the share
//   of its resources that grow here and by its yield, except an Always one; a Grazed clue's by the grazing;
//   a Scavenge clue's by predatorBoost when predators are near, and none is noticed whose animals all range elsewhere.
// tutorials: once-per-game lines, by id. searchBands: how a tile's search effort reads, against the time
//   a thorough search of its terrain takes (the longest expected find in its draws), lowest first.
